# Cline Rules

- Only read files directly relevant to the current task.
- Do not scan the entire repository.
- Do not inspect node_modules, .git, build, dist, coverage, or generated files.
- Before reading a file, determine whether it is necessary.
- Prefer editing the smallest number of files possible.
- Do not run unnecessary commands.
- Do not repeat commands whose output has already been obtained.
- Keep terminal commands focused and concise.
- For simple coding tasks, make the change directly instead of exploring unrelated files.
